# decision package.json receives precise dependency edits

The npm adapter changes only the matching `dependencies` entry. Existing inline JSON keeps its
surrounding bytes and unrelated dependencies; no whole-document pretty-print is allowed.
Locked wiring uses the canonical Git URL plus the full locked commit, and drift reads
`package.json` even when no package lock exists.
All Git dependencies use an explicit `git+` transport. In particular, Yarn Berry receives
`git+ssh://...#commit=<sha>` (with SCP-style SSH URLs normalised first); bare `ssh://` and
`https://` selectors are not valid Yarn Git dependencies.

# decision npm refresh cannot run lifecycle scripts

When `package-lock.json` exists, refresh uses `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts
--no-audit --no-fund`. Without a package lock it performs no command. Yarn Berry, pnpm, and Bun
use their dependency-specific native update command.

# test npm adapter preservation

- Wire and unwire are idempotent and preserve unrelated inline JSON bytes.
- Tampering with the manifest pin is drift even without `package-lock.json`.
- npm refresh is lockfile-only and disables scripts, audit, and funding requests.
- Yarn Berry output carries a `git+` transport for HTTPS, SSH, and SCP-style inputs.
